 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Cells A1..Z100, all initially 0. Inferred exact-numeric domain: a cell holds a non-negative decimal integer literal (<=10^6) or a formula \"=\" t1 \"+\" t2 ... (1..20 terms) where each term is a cell reference or such a literal. getCell evaluates live (references reflect later edits) and returns an integer; resetCell restores 0. Inference narrows the source's double values to integers so both languages are exact; results above 2^53-1 are outside the inferred domain. Level 1 inputs never create a circular reference.",
  "provenance": [
